<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  RUT_KraytAttack.xml                     RimUtinni — STILLSAND_EVENT_CREATURES_1 §2

  The krayt attack: a krayt dragon comes up out of the Stillsand and fights on the surface.
  Owner, typed, volley turn 2: "This biome needs event level creatures. Attacks by the mighty
  krayt dragon. And others." Owner, by card, 2026-09-30: the krayts and the war wyrm STAY
  WILD (WildAnimals_Stillsand.xml is unchanged); this attack is added on top.

  XML only. The worker is the RM tier's RimMandrake.Stillsand.RM_IncidentWorker_SandLeviathan
  (src/RimMandrake/Stillsand/Source/RM_SandLeviathan.cs), which never names a krayt; the
  krayt is data here (Q11a: canon IP lives in the Utinni layer). surfaceFighter makes it
  manhunter on arrival. It dives once fed (taking the body down a drag line into a funnel),
  on fire, or after hardGroundGiveUpTicks off the sand.

  Gate: all three mods by MayRequire (the worker's mod, the krayt's mod, and the sand-swim kit
  the krayt's own RM_SandSwimExtension needs). Biome by defName in the extension. Toggle and
  odds: Mod Settings, "Stillsand: event creatures" (rows are built from every IncidentDef on
  this worker). Weighted up by vibration (powered deep drills). The Return's Debt weighting
  is owed to STILLSAND_RETURN_RITUAL_1.
-->
<Defs>

  <IncidentDef MayRequire="mandrake.rm.stillsand,mandrake.rsw.swbestiary,mandrake.rm.creaturebehaviors">
    <defName>RUT_KraytAttack</defName>
    <label>krayt attack</label>
    <workerClass>RimMandrake.Stillsand.RM_IncidentWorker_SandLeviathan</workerClass>
    <category>ThreatBig</category>
    <letterDef>ThreatBig</letterDef>
    <letterLabel>Krayt dragon</letterLabel>
    <letterText>Something vast is moving under the sand.\n\nThe ground is humming on the windward horizon, louder every minute. A krayt dragon is coming, and it is heading for whatever is making the most noise.\n\nIt will break the surface and fight. Kill it, or make it dive: it will not stay long on rock, it will not stand in fire, and once it has fed it takes what it caught down with it.</letterText>
    <baseChance>0.6</baseChance>
    <minRefireDays>40</minRefireDays>
    <earliestDay>20</earliestDay>
    <minThreatPoints>800</minThreatPoints>
    <pointsScaleable>false</pointsScaleable>
    <targetTags>
      <li>Map_PlayerHome</li>
      <li>Map_TempIncident</li>
    </targetTags>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="RimMandrake.Stillsand.RM_SandLeviathanExtension">
        <biomes>
          <li>RM_Stillsand</li>
        </biomes>
        <pawnKind>RSW_KraytDragon</pawnKind>
        <surfaceFighter>true</surfaceFighter>
        <warningTicks>2000</warningTicks>
        <maxStayTicks>30000</maxStayTicks>
        <hardGroundGiveUpTicks>1200</hardGroundGiveUpTicks>
        <breachRingRadius>4.9</breachRingRadius>
        <breachStaggerTicks>120</breachStaggerTicks>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
  </IncidentDef>

</Defs>
